    <summary>Open-source PDF editor for Windows with text editing, OCR, annotations, redaction, signatures, forms, Office export and page organization.</summary>
    <description>PDF editor for Windows. View, annotate, OCR, merge, split, edit text, draw, sign, fill forms, redact, protect, convert, print, flatten, and open password-protected PDFs without an Adobe subscription or telemetry.

**Features:**

- Rendering, text extraction, search, editing and document processing through KillerPDF's own PDF engine
- Four view modes (Single, Continuous, Two-Page with a book layout option, Grid), tabbed documents that restore their page, zoom and view mode, and a split pane (F10) for two documents side by side
- Sidebar panels for pages, outline, comments, attachments, layers and signatures, dockable on any side of the window; tabs at the top or the bottom
- Edit a page's own text line by line or by paragraph, with font matching, or change matching text everywhere with Find and Replace
- Text boxes, freehand drawing, lines, shapes, highlights, strikethrough, underline, stamps and images, with an RGB color picker and screen eyedropper
- Calibrated Distance, Perimeter, Area and Angle measurements with units, snapping and a report
- Built-in OCR, no cloud: OCR a page or region to the clipboard, make a searchable PDF, or convert a scan to real text; languages download on demand
- Export to Word, Excel, PowerPoint, HTML, Markdown, text, JSON and page images, with reviewed table export to XLSX or CSV; convert Word and Excel files to PDF; scan through TWAIN
- Permanent redaction by area, text search or sensitive-data pattern, with verification and optional sanitization
- Protect copies with passwords, permissions or certificate recipients; restricted PDFs open read-only and unlock with the owner password
- Form filling with live text, checkbox, radio, dropdown and comb fields; recognize fields, flatten forms, and exchange FDF and XFDF data
- Digital signatures from a Windows certificate or .pfx file with RFC 3161 timestamps; verify signers, certificate chains and later changes
- Compare two documents with the changes marked; merge, split, extract, reorder, rotate, reverse, straighten and divide scanned spreads
- Correct a photographed page's perspective, adjust color and levels, crop with handles, and rasterize a region
- Headers, footers, page numbers, watermarks and Bates batches; N-up, booklet and poster layouts; preflight, accessibility and print-production reports; Reduce File Size
- Guided tasks, reusable macros, watched folders and data merge from CSV, JSON or XLSX
- Full command line with scripting-friendly exit codes for merging, splitting, rendering, printing, OCR, redaction, export and batch work
- Bookmark editing, table of contents generation, page labels, full-text search, and column-aware text selection
- Undo and redo across annotations, page operations and document edits
- Print with a real in-app preview (paper, scale, margins, pages per sheet, two-sided)
- Optional File Explorer and Outlook PDF previews for installed copies
- Thirteen themes and 41 looks, twenty languages, interface scaling, custom shortcuts, and Search Tools (Ctrl+K)
- Compact installer (per-user or machine-wide, uses the .NET 10 Desktop Runtime) or a self-contained portable download
- GPLv3, local-only, no account, no telemetry
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/SteveTheKiller/KillerPDF/releases/tag/vREPLACE_VERSION</releaseNotes>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="dotnet-10.0-desktopruntime" version="[10.0.0,11.0.0)" />
    </dependencies>
